THE DAILY CHAOS OF A DYING MEGASTRUCTURE

(25s · 9:16 · 18 Scenes)

STYLE & LOOK

Hyper-detailed sci-fi hyper-realism with illustrated texture.
Dense vertical city-organism fused with machines, creatures, scaffolding, cables, and weapons.
Color palette: toxic teal skies, rusted metal, coral reds, bio-blue glows, dirty yellows.
Camera language: whip pans, vertical dollies, micro push-ins, snap zooms.
No slow shots. No stillness. Chaos is routine.

GLOBAL ACTION RULES (HARD CONSTRAINTS)

Motion is never decorative.
Every movement must interact, collide, interrupt, or escalate.

• Spores slam into surfaces, obscuring vision
• Cables snap, whip, or drag objects
• Creatures recoil, lunge, detach, or block paths
• Steam blasts violently, knocking people back
• Debris falls with consequence — causing reactions below
No idle loops. No ambient drift.
If something moves, someone reacts.

GLOBAL MOTION RULES

• Every level shows a different survival task
• No transformations — only things reacting
• Creatures blink, breathe, recoil, observe
• Weapons recoil, reload, misfire
• Micro SFX synced to action: hisses, clicks, radio static, alien chirps, distant explosions
• Camera never stops moving — like a war correspondent falling downward

ABSOLUTE RULE:
First frame must contain motion, collision, or active threat.
No establishing shots. No calm wide views.
Camera enters mid-action as if already filming.

CAMERA & TIMING CONSTRAINTS (ANTI-FREEZE)

• No shot longer than 1.4 seconds
• No static framing — camera must be:

falling
being pulled
dodging obstacles
shaken by impacts

• If the camera slows, something hits frame immediately
• No locked-off shots

PHYSICS-FIRST RULE
If motion does not change the situation, it is forbidden.
Examples:
Steam must block vision or burn
Smoke must be displaced by shockwaves
Creatures must interfere with movement
Falling objects must trigger secondary chaos

OPENING-SPECIFIC OVERRIDE (Frame 1 Rule)

First frame must already be mid-impact.
The camera enters during:
an explosion aftermath
a weapon firing
a structure failing
a collision in progress
No establishing shots.
No beauty passes.
No “world introduction.”


SCENE LIST (Top → Bottom descent)
SCENE 1 (0.0–1.2s) — Sky Debris Corridor

High-altitude wide.
Alien spores, drifting wreckage, distant air battles.
Small fighters streak past, leaving ion trails.

(SFX: distant engines, wind howl)

SCENE 2 (1.2–2.3s) — Watcher Organisms

Push past massive coral-like creatures embedded in walls.
Their eyes track the camera independently.

(SFX: wet blinking, low hum)

SCENE 3 (2.3–3.4s) — Scavenger Rig Level

Humans in patchwork armor welding, stripping alien tech.
