(SFX: suction roar, bone crunch)

SCENE 13 (13.6–14.8s) — Command Balcony

Officer shouting orders over holographic map.
Map glitches violently as reality disagrees.

(SFX: glitch stutter, shouted coordinates)

SCENE 14 (14.8–16.0s) — Collapse Near-Miss

Whole platform tilts.
Everyone leans instinctively — nothing collapses.
They continue working.

(SFX: metal groan, relieved exhale)

SCENE 15 (16.0–17.3s) — Last Stand Corridor

Multiple soldiers firing downward.
Muzzle flashes strobe the entire frame.

(SFX: automatic fire, echoing screams)

SCENE 16 (17.3–18.6s) — Tourist With Camera

Someone calmly filming everything.
Camera shakes violently — they keep recording.

(SFX: camera shutter + chaos)

SCENE 17 (18.6–20.0s) — WIDE REVEAL, BUT UNSTABLE

Fast crane back begins — but the world fights it.

• Fighters tear past camera toward the structure
• Two explosions ripple across different levels
• One alien creature detaches and falls downward through frame
• Smoke columns bend sideways from shockwaves

Camera is pulled back, not floating freely.

(SFX: engines tearing past, overlapping explosions, air distortion)

SCENE 18 (20.0–21.2s) — CHAIN REACTION

Without cutting:

• A lower platform collapses → debris rains down
• Zipline snaps → two figures swing wildly, barely holding
• A weapon misfires → sparks cascade vertically
• Lights flicker across the entire structure like a nervous system firing

Camera continues retreating — faster now.

(SFX: metal shearing, screams swallowed by distance)

SCENE 19 (21.2–22.6s) — SCALE ATTACK

Hard cut to a slightly wider angle (not the final one yet):

• Multiple ships converge from different depths
• Defensive fire erupts from the structure in all directions
• One ship explodes mid-air, shockwave warping smoke and debris
• Creatures recoil simultaneously — like the building flinched

(Music peaks, chaotic but rhythmic)

SCENE 19 (22.6–24.5s) — NO RESOLUTION

Another cut — even wider:

• The megastructure keeps functioning despite everything
• New figures appear where others fell
• Fires burn, repairs begin immediately, fighting continues
• Life does NOT slow down

Camera finally reaches maximum distance at 24.5s —
motion everywhere, no “final pose.”

(Music abruptly CUTS at 24.5s)

SCENE 20 (24.5–25.0s) — TEXT HIT (SEPARATE SCENE)
Hard cut to black.
Text appears instantly, dead center:
IT’S JUST LIFE.

Single distorted guitar hit.
No fade.
End.